tests/ir/cholesky_through_a_name.sky:6:5: note: `A⁻¹ @ b` is rewritten to a Cholesky solve
  |
6 | B = inv(A)
  |     ^^^^^^
  = note: rewrite `A⁻¹ @ b` to a Cholesky solve: A is Matrix[3,3] and PositiveDefinite, b is Vector[3]. Factor A = L·Lᵀ (L lower-triangular), solve L·y = b, then Lᵀ·x = y. x = A⁻¹·b is Vector[3]; A⁻¹ is still computed for its other users.
  = note: applied by the `cholesky` pass
